<title>FRANCE: EU grants soft wheat at 16.59 Ecus/T rebate - ONIC.</title>
<headline>EU grants soft wheat at 16.59 Ecus/T rebate - ONIC.</headline>
<text>
<p>PARIS, Nov 21 (reuter) - The European Union on Thursday granted 311,300 tonnes of free-market soft wheat at a maximum refund of 16.59 Ecus per tonne, France's grain office ONIC confirmed.</p>
<p>Earlier, member country officials had put the refund at around 16.50 Ecus per tonne.  </p>
<p>The EU also granted licences to export 268,000 tonnes of free-market barley at a maximum refund of 31.49 Ecus per tonne, ONIC said.</p>
<p>The EU's grain management committee in Brussels also agreed the export of 17,000 tonnes of free-market rye at the same refund of 31.49 Ecus per tonne and of 1,500 tonnes of oats at a refund of 32.80 Ecus per tonne, it said.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
